      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1,700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is double the maximum labeled metformin dose. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nIt may be a typo or a mix-up between the per-dose and daily totals. Possible intended orders include:\n\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day divided.** For example, 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** These are common regimens.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that, and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it."
      }
     ],
